The Baden @-@ Württemberg Landscape Law Directive ( LPR ) enables the state to support wheat fences .
The goal is to keep the Black Forest open .
The precondition is the existence of a promotion framework designated by the LPR .
In addition , the fence area must not be traceable ( slope over 35 % ) and must therefore be threatened by afforestation .
The application for the Weidezaunprojekt 2010 in Fischerbacher is currently being applied by eight participants with 24 plots , who want to build a fence of almost 16 kilometres .
The open area is 35 hectares , the calculated cost is more than 112 000 euros .
Is nothing more sacred ?
Now the White House of Trump is accepting the Statue of Liberty .
The surest sign of a change of regime is when they start attacking the statues .
The Americans appreciate it as much as any other - hence the carefully staged fall of Saddam Hussein in Baghdad &apos;s Firdos Square in 2003 .
Stephen Miller , one of the key ideologists of the Trumpius regime , knew for sure what he was doing when he took a symbolic axe with a heated dispute with Jim Acosta of CNN about the President &apos;s proposals to drastically limit legal immigration to the Statue of Liberty .
To be fair , Miller did not attack the statue himself .
A crowd of boat owners and Liberty imitators would have lynched him had he done so .
But he attacked their meaning , and especially the meaning they were attributed to them when the famous poem by Emma Lazarus was added to his base 17 years after the monument was completed .
When Miller Acosta cried : &quot; I don &apos;t want to go into a whole thing about history here , but the statue of freedom is ... a symbol of American freedom that illuminates the world .
The poem to which you refer , which was added later and is not part of the original Statue of Liberty . &quot;
Miller is factually correct , but as he himself said , it is not really about history .
It is about the contemporary response to the arousal words of Lazarus , the only one where a state invites not only any old immigrants , but the poorest of the poor : &quot; Your tiredness , your poor , your afflicted masses who yearn to breathe freely / the miserable waste of your rich coasts . &quot;
There was never a time when the &quot; miserable waste &quot; could be seen better on our screens .
Miller did not engage in literary criticism - he made it clear that these people in the USA are not welcome .
This conflict because of the importance of a statue is part of a broader political and cultural conflict : it is indeed a conflict about the meaning of America .
Lazarus - and her friends who were working to place their words at the base after their death - knew very well that they were doing a highly political act .
The sculpture was to show the connections between French and American Republicanism , by depicting the female embodiment of freedom in a worn @-@ out classical visual representation .
Lazarus changed this meaning : in her poem , the female figure is no longer abstract - she has received a voice .
And she gives herself a completely different name : the mother of the exiles .
The combination of poems and images is a brilliant feminist coup and a disastrous attack on American nativism .
And just as Lazarus changed the meaning of the statue , the people on the right wing wanted to change it a long time ago .
The great scribe Rush Limbaugh , a kind of John the Baptist for the coming of a new ticketing of a new man , argued in 2010 that the Statue of Liberty would not invite anyone , but rather would be an early neo @-@ conservative who brought the American flame to the night @-@ time world : &quot; Lady Liberty is moving forward .
It is said to carry the torch of freedom from the United States to the rest of the world .
The torch should not illuminate the path to the United States . &quot;
Limbaugh was hit by something quite unusual .
The meaning of the statue is a question of perception &apos;s point of view .
The great fantasy of Lazarus was to see it as seen by the exhausted , miserable , but hopeful people after long and often terrible journeys on the decks of ships .
In the truest sense , it is about seeing the world from the perspective of people who seek refuge and an opportunity to improve their lives .
Her statue speaks to them the words of hope and welcome they must hear .
And this is not the perspective Miller and Trump would ever like to acknowledge .
Their torch is not to illuminate the path , but to ignite the hatred , which is their only source of power .
