Less lung cancer deaths due to passive smoking
In the past two decades , fewer and fewer people have died from lung cancer due to passive smoking .
This is the conclusion reached by scientists from the Hamburg @-@ Eppendorf University Hospital ( UKE ) in a study .
&quot; According to our estimates , 167 lung cancer deaths per year are attributable to passive smoking , &quot; said Heiko Becher , Chief of Studies .
He also made a comparison with a study of his own on this subject from 1994 .
At that time , there were still 400 lung cancer deaths per year due to passive smoking in Germany .
The new study is published in the International Journal of Public Health .
