More than 1 in 5 US travellers bring forbidden objects to the plane , finds a survey out .
A survey of air passengers revealed that more than 20 percent of objects that were deliberately or unintentionally banned were smuggled past the control points of the US Transportation Security Administration , including at least 6 percent that entered the plane , while they accidentally wore prohibited knives or other objects with blades .
Less than 1 % claimed they had been late in discovering that they had mistakenly traveled with firearms , ammunition or explosives .
The survey of more than 1,000 people - carried out by a Jet charterservice , Stratos Jet Charters Inc . - also revealed that younger travellers tend to ignore the rules .
The survey &apos;s decision to admit that they had knowingly tried to fly with something prohibited by the TSA was to see 19.7 percent millennials , compared to less than 15 percent , members of Generation X .
The most frequent objects that were deliberately passed through to TSA agents were food and liquids .
More than 3 % admitted that they knowingly carried objects with blades through the security check , while 2.2 % of the women surveyed and 3.7 % of male respondents also confirmed that they had brought intentionally banned drugs onto the plane .
The company said it had interviewed travellers throughout the country to find out how many had accidentally smuggled goods through airport security and how many had intentionally done it .
It is no surprise that the people who wear smuggling goods most - knowingly or unknowingly - through security were the ones who fly the most frequently .
The company points out , however , that the TSA guidelines are somewhat complicated and confusing .
People are often uncertain which liquids they are allowed to carry with them or how much of it .
It is therefore no surprise that the largest quantity of liquids prohibited by the TSA are liquids .
For a while people thought that the TSA could consider books as smuggling goods .
Liquids are allowed on domestic flights , but not on international flights .
Elon Musk doesn &apos;t care : tens of thousands of Tesla customers cancel the order .
Elon Musk , Elon Musk Electric @-@ Thousand , is happy to announce the huge number of pre @-@ orders for his new Tesla &quot; Model 3 . &quot;
In this context , he has hitherto failed to mention that some of the customers have already withdrawn their non @-@ binding reservation .
