Pearson is cutting another 3,000 jobs and is cutting the dividend to revitalise the business .
Pearson , the UK educational group , said on Friday that it would cut 3,000 more jobs and cut its interim dividend by 72 % , as a further restructuring program was launched to overcome the pressure the company was faced with .
The job cuts announced by General Director John Fallon for the most part for the end of 2018 and early 2019 are in addition to his previous restructuring , in which 4,000 jobs had already been lost .
In May Pearson announced in a third cost @-@ cutting program a cost @-@ cutting plan of another £ 300m ( $ 394 million ) to revitalise a business taken by the fast step towards digital learning .
Sale as a distributor of Penguin Random House &apos;s stake in Bertelsmann last month , the company said that the outlook for the financial year was unchanged , having achieved an increase of 1 percent to £ 2.05 billion in the first half of the year .
Kabul Convoi : Nato soldier killed in suicide bombing
A suicide bomber attacked a military convoy in the Afghan capital Kabul , killed one soldier of Nato and injured several others , say officials .
Five soldiers and an interpreter had been injured , announced a statement by Nato .
Unconfirmed local reports have shown that three civilians died in the Qarabagh district .
The bombing is the last act of violence that Afghanistan suffered this month - more than 30 people were killed in a mosque in Herat on Tuesday .
On Monday , a suicide bomber killed two people near the Iraqi Embassy in Kabul .
Nato &apos;s statement states that the explosion on Thursday evening occurred when a joint patrol with the Afghan army was &quot; attacked &quot; by an improvised explosive kit worn by persons .
The statement says that all the injured are in a stable condition and are treated in the US military hospital at the Bagram Airfield .
Correspondents say that the growing strength of the Taliban and the group known as the Islamic State ( IS ) in Qarabagh is a major concern for NATO troops in the nearby Bagram .
According to the United Nations , in the first half of 2017 , Afghanistan suffered at least 1,662 civil deaths , of which approximately 20 % were in the capital .
At the end of July , a suicide car bomb killed at least 30 people in a mainly Shiite district of Kabul .
The Taliban said they had carried out this attack .
On May 31 , a massive bombing in the city centre killed more than 150 people with the most deadly military attack in the country since the US @-@ led troops supplanted the Taliban from power in 2001 .
The violence highlights the precarious security situation in Afghanistan , as US President Donald Trump is weighing up the number of US troops supporting the military and the police in the country .
Correspondents say that suicide attacks in Kabul in recent weeks have also caused a crisis of public trust in the government , its policies and , in particular , the call of President Ashraf Ghani .
EPO reverts decision to delay the smog rule after lawsuits .
The U.S. Environmental Protection Agency has annulled a decision to delay a regulation of Obama &apos;s government requiring states to reduce smog @-@ causing emissions one day after 15 countries sued the agency for the move .
The EPO announced late on Wednesday the decision to push ahead with the so @-@ called &quot; ozone provisions 2015 , &quot; and said that it would indicate the agency &apos;s commitment to cooperate with states .
&quot; We believe in dialogue with and in our responsiveness to our state partners , &quot; said EPO Chief Scott Pruitt in a statement .
Pruitt announced in June that EPO would delay by one year until October 2018 the ozone regulations - in which harmful emissions are to be measured in one part of the country , in order to determine where reductions need to be made to meet stricter air quality standards .
A group of 15 largely democratic states , together with the district of Colombia , filed a lawsuit on Tuesday saying that the effort was illegal .
President Donald Trump &apos;s government has tried to cut back a broad range of environmental demands imposed by former president Barack Obama as part of a broader agenda that , according to him , should boost economic growth .
The efforts , however , have triggered the setback of the democrats and nature conservation groups , who are worried about the impact of major emissions on public health .
The EPO website states that inhaling air containing ozone can &quot; reduce lung function and increase respiratory symptoms &quot; such as asthma .
