Agricultural Minister in an interview - How do we protect ourselves from poison buckets , Mr. Schmidt ?
Germany discusses contaminated eggs .
How could the scandal happen ?
How can consumers protect themselves .
Agricultural Minister Christian Schmidt ( CSU ) is in interview with the editorial network Deutschland ( RND ) .
Mr. Schmidt , How can the consumer protect himself from poisoned eggs ?
I can only encourage all consumers to look closely at the eggs in their fridge and verify the stamp .
On the consumer protection portal www.medizinalung.de the federal states provide the latest information about the eggs charts concerned .
Affected eggs should be destroyed or returned .
Even if , according to all we know at the moment , a health hazard is virtually impossible .
Does Aldi now take over the best possible crisis response - all eggs are taken out of the offer - because the central role of the Enlightenment is not really perceived by the Federal Minister of Agriculture ?
Food surveillance is the responsibility of the federal states .
Nevertheless , my house has been up @-@ dated immediately and has been in close contact with the authorities of the countries since the German concern was announced .
All information and risk assessment are available to consumers .
The retail trade , like the manufacturers , must ensure that the products sold are marketable and do not present any health hazards .
If eggs have exceeded the maximum residue limit of 0.005mg / kg , they are not marketable .
Unpolluted eggs , however , can be sold and consumed .
This time it is not the fault of the companies .
Are production and consumer seats in the same boat ?
At present , the production companies are not directly to blame .
Instead , they are expected to suffer economic damage due to the alleged illegal practices of service companies .
As always , there are not enough controllers in the worst case .
Is it only the personnel or the coherent competence that is missing ?
It was the official controls that revealed the process .
The truth is , however , that food fraud and criminal energy can never be 100 % excluded .
For this reason , it is of vital importance to provide a consistent clarification of such events and to hand them over to the prosecution in cases where criminal offences may occur .
I have already made it clear on several occasions that I expect the responsible authorities to provide a complete explanation .
Is regular alarmism really necessary in the event of food scandals ?
Consumers have the right to obtain only safe and marketable foods .
When an unauthorized insecticide is used in the food industry , consumers are rightly outraged .
The panelled means put manufacturers , traders and consumers in a situation that is absolutely not necessary .
In principle , it must be clear that the illegal use of the insecticide Fipronil in the preparation of food @-@ producing animals is not acceptable and must be terminated immediately .
This requires consistent and high @-@ pressure work at all levels .
I expect all the competent authorities to investigate the matter quickly and seamlessly .
What effect the Financial Rules of the Football have on Neymar &apos;s move to Paris ?
The rules that aim to prevent unhindered expenses of the European football clubs will not disrupt Neymars world record transfer from Barcelona to Paris @-@ Saint Germain , France .
Any consequences will still come for Paris Saint @-@ Germain from UEFA , because the senior organization that has supervised the European game has the power to ban teams from access to the prestigious Champions League tournament .
Financial Fair Play Rules , which were initiated by UEFA in 2011 , mean that PSG will eventually have to prove that Neymar &apos;s transfer was financed without any major losses .
Barcelona has paid 222 million euros ( $ 262 million ) to buy the Brazilian out of his contract , and Neymar will receive a salary that will be several tens of millions of dollars a year .
Here are some of the financial aspects of Neymars move to France .
PSG can certainly make money loose so that Neymar signs and brings him to a galaxy of other stars , given the financing of the team by the energetic ruling family of Qatar .
Clubs may spend a lot of money on the acquisition of players , but must counteract with legitimate revenue sources that allow them to break even point in their football @-@ related business .
FFP was conceived by Michel Platini after his election as UEFA President in 2007 .
The former French player believed that clubs that had incurred enormous debts in their quest for success would effectively cheat and risk ruining themselves when banks or owners withdraw their support .
In 2011 FFP moved from concentrating on club debts to monitoring their losses . The company was not able to maintain its position as a manager of the club .
The change meant that the business model Roman Abramovich used in Chelsea in 2003 - buying a club with potential and then investing heavily to improve the team and build a global brand - was to become a harder business .
During the current three @-@ year FFP investment period , which runs until 2018 , clubs may suffer losses of € 30 million .
And although Platini fell in disfavor from the presidency in 2015 , his successor UEFA , Aleksander Ceferin , is still working to discourage excessive spending .
&quot; Certainly FFP is not dead and we are certain to reinforce the rules for the future , &quot; Andrea Traverso , UEFA &apos;s manager for FFP , told The Associated Press last week .
Although the PSG has paid Neymar &apos;s buy @-@ out clause in a lump @-@ sum , it may distribute the amount for the accounting for the duration of its contract .
Neymar has signed a five @-@ year contract , so that the deductions for the next five years amounting to EUR 44.4 million can be recorded in the annual financial statements .
The first wave of FFP sanctions in 2014 , together with Abu Dhabi , owned by Manchester City , the PSG hit the heaviest sanctions .
The PSG was fined 60 million euros ( at that time $ 82 million ) , which was later reduced to 20 million euros - and was ordered that the team members for the Champions League for the 2014 / 15 season remain limited to 21 players instead of the usual 25 players .
UEFA is looking for clubs to try to outwit their financial supervision by leveraging their revenues from companies associated with the owners of a club .
While a Catalan company could sponsor the PSG if the value of sponsoring should exceed the standard market rates , UEFA would not allow this to be considered a legitimate income .
This is exactly what happened in 2014 , when the UEFA decided that the value of sponsoring the PSA was inflated by the Qatar Tourism Authority .
It was reported that part of the PSG payments to Neymar could come to Qatar from the Organizing Committee of the 2022 World Cup .
But PSG and Qatar 2022 have denied that Neymar will become World Cup ambassador and that such a manoeuvre could be easy to find out for the UEFA regulatory authorities .
The previous sanctions against PSG mean that UEFA will be even more attentive to any attempt to circumvent the rules .
UEFA had no preliminary discussions with PSG on Neymars Transfer , and on Thursday they told the people familiar with the situation .
They spoke with The Associated Press on the condition of anonymity , because they were not authorized to discuss the PSG situation .
The latest reports show that PSG 2015 / 16 has achieved a profit of more than 10 million euros with revenues of 542.4 million euros .
The accounts for the last financial year have yet to be published .
PSG expects Neymar &apos;s arrival to be a blessing for sponsoring deals , merchandising and trick sales .
The association expects that after signing the contract , sales will increase by at least 30 % .
The Spanish League was clearly irritated to see one of the best football players go , and it tried to prevent Neymars leaving by claiming that PSG would violate FFP .
&quot; It is a clear case of &quot; financial doping &quot; with the club and the state , &quot; said the president of the La Liga , Javier Tebas , the Spanish daily AS in relation to Qatar &apos;s final ownership to PSG .
Arsenal manager Arsene Wenger , whose club owns an American sports tycoon , shares the reservations of La Liga against a state that finances an association .
&quot; It is the consequence of ownership and this has completely changed the entire football landscape in the last 15 years , &quot; Wenger said on Thursday .
&quot; As soon as a country owns an association , everything is possible .
It will be very difficult to respect financial fair play because you go different ways or may have different interests , if a country has such a large player to represent a country . &quot;
