Italy tightens the tone on NGO migrants rescue boats
Italy has warned NGOs that use lifeguards for migrants in the Mediterranean that they cannot continue to do so unless they comply with new rules for their operations .
&quot; If NGOs do not sign a new code of conduct , it is difficult to see how they can continue to work , &quot; said Interior Minister Marco Minniti in an interview with Turin daily La Stampa .
Minnitis &apos;s warning came one day after the Italian authorities had seized a boat of the German charity &quot; Jugend Rettet &quot; because their team had worked effectively with people @-@ traders in a way that facilitated illegal immigration .
The charity , which has been in operation for a year , refused to comment on the detailed accusations of the Italian prosecutor Ambrogio Cartosio .
