The crew is suspected of flouting the authority of the Italian Coastguard , which monitors rescue operations in the area for humanitarian reasons and not for any other reason .
Under the code of conduct , boats such as Iuventa must have an Italian police officer on board who supervises their activities .
Only three of the nine NGOs involved in search and rescue operations have agreed to abide by the code : Save the Children , MOAS from Malta and Pro @-@ Activa Open Arms from Spain .
The latter said on Thursday that the new rules would be deemed unnecessary but acceptable , as they would not bring &quot; significant changes or obstructions &quot; to their rescue operations .
Among those who refuse to sign is the Nobel Prize winner organisation MSF . The MSF is the MSF of the German MSF .
Minniti meanwhile said that the number of migrants arriving in Italy after the rescue activities has declined sharply in the last weeks , indicating that efforts to strengthen the Libyan Coast Guard and to cooperate with local mayors have borne fruit .
&quot; In the last few days we have started to see light at the end of the tunnel , &quot; the minister said .
