For many , the performance will require getting used to .
Ingo Frobösschen has also been dealing with the question for a long time .
For the professor at the German Sporthochschule in Cologne e @-@ sport is a sport because it is competitive and it shows many biological and physical reactions which you can also find in classical sports - for example , increased heart frequencies , stress reactions , hormonal changes .
Cognitive skills , technical and tactical understanding and rapid reaction capabilities are also required .
Professional gamers should not only train at the console but also at their bodies and take care of the diet .
&quot; The fittest player is a good player . &quot;
Frobatic also sees problems : &quot; Doping is becoming more and more a topic . &quot;
The controls were difficult to carry out in online games and the structures of classical sports were missing in the scene .
The scientist highlights the high integrative effect of e @-@ sports in a positive way .
Players are traveling internationally , this is like a large global family , there are no intercultural barriers .
A study by Deloitte , the consulting firm , and the German Federal Association of Interactive Entertainment Software ( BIU ) predicts rapid growth in e @-@ sport .
