But thanks to the crazy number of - I think - senseless construction projects in Bitburg , there is no room for a farmhouse market hall .
When the farmhouse market hall is destroyed , a piece of culture will disappear again . &quot;
A fitting similarity : the artist creates portraits with Chelsea Mannings DNA .
In the center of the Fridman Gallery in New York , there are many faces - white , black and brown , which are almost imperceptibly alike - hanging from the ceiling on the cables .
The 30 portraits were created by the artist Heather Dewey @-@ Hagborg , made of cheeky tubs and haircuts sent to her by Chelsea Manning .
Manning sent the excerpts from Fort Leavenworth , where the former intelligence analyst served a 35 @-@ year prison sentence after publishing secret diplomatic messages on the WikiLeaks website .
The new exhibition , which opened on August 2 , is called A Becoming Resemblance .
She is the product of two years of correspondence between Dewey @-@ Hagborg , whose discipline united their expertise in technology , computer science and art , and Manning , a transwoman and groundbreaking dissident whose condemnation was transformed by Barack Obama when he was in his office for only three days .
Dewey @-@ Hagborg , by analysing the DNA extraction from Manning , which has created 30 portraits of how someone could look with these genomic data , has created a sharp , if somewhat intellectual comment not only on the formability of DNA data - the many ways in which they can be interpreted and the inherent determinism of these interpretations - but also on identity .
Manning , who was born Bradley Edward but has already spoken openly about the identification as a woman since her puberty , was convicted in 2013 for 20 charges , including six crimes against the spying law , computer fraud and theft .
Through the prison , her image was suppressed , so much so that there was only one photo - a silky , black and white selfie in which Manning is apparently sitting on a driver &apos;s seat and wearing a platinblonde persert - with which she was associated .
In 2015 Dewey @-@ Hagborg just came out of the great success of her 2012 project &apos; Stranger Visions &apos; .
In this , the artist produced portraits of strangers from forensic artifacts like cigarette sleeves and chewing gum , extracting DNA from the waste to give an idea of what these people might look like .
That was the time when she received an email from a newspaper magazine .
&quot; They conducted an interview with Chelsea Manning while in prison , and they wanted a kind of portrait to accompany this article , &quot; Dewey @-@ Hagborg explained during a press preview of the new exhibition .
And she couldn &apos;t be visited at that time and she could not be photographed , so you contacted Chelsea and asked her if she wanted to make a DNA portrait .
The artist and her imprisoned Muse were turned into unequal circles of peppers , who exchanged several letters over the course of two years .
They even created a comic book &quot; Suppressed Images , &quot; illustrated by Shoili Kanungo , which predicted a future in which the president would transform the judgement and enable him to see the exhibition in person .
That Obama would indeed demand Mannings &apos; release just a few days after the book was published after seven brutal years in a military prison in Kansas was a welcome kind of happy meeting .
There is still a bit of depth and strength in the opening of the exhibition , as Donald Trump is waging a war against informants from the government camp and against Transgender troops to find new ways to further inflame the rigid divisions he was supposed to resolve .
When Dewey @-@ Hagborg was asked about the strange timing of all these things , she said that &quot; things happen for a certain reason . &quot;
In an artistic statement written on the wall of the gallery , Manning , with its oversized signature underlining ( the &quot; i &quot; in her surname is bearing a heart ) , called for an end to the &quot; automatic fragmentation , based on gender , race , sexuality and culture . &quot;
On the opposite wall , her mitochondrial DNA sequence - a thousand foot @-@ scorer of Cs and Gs and Aces - is written in pencil .
Dewey @-@ Hagborg hoped to show by including the 200 letters ( or nucleotides according to the artist &apos;s sophisticated scientific lexicon ) how amazingly similar , at least in biological terms , we are all .
&quot; What people hopefully will take with them is that our genome does not care who we are and how open genetic data are for an interpretation and how subjective they are , &quot; said Dewey @-@ Hagborg , whose video work of 2007 , Spurious Memories , is also visible .
&quot; DNA data can tell so many different stories , so that &apos;s why they are 30 of those stories . &quot;
The last piece in the exhibition , which is kept in a separate room , is a page from the above @-@ mentioned comic novel .
She shows Manning how she appears with a hands @-@ free phone from the disciplines of the United States like King @-@ Kong .
&quot; When they put your speech to cold , they won , &quot; it is said .
&quot; So never stop the mouth . &quot;
&quot; It came directly from a letter she wrote to me , &quot; said the artist who greets Philadelphia .
&quot; I still get goose bumper when I talk about it . &quot;
Manning has not seen the exhibition personally yet - as it was anticipated in the comic book - but if she does , then in the middle of the room she will be greeted by the masks , her own genomic sicilian , who join together like hordes of protesters .
This was also targeted , like everything in the exhibition , to the size ( 5 &quot; 2 , Mannings Statur ) , where their genetic hippos were written with pencil .
&quot; In the past I had them on the wall , but I wanted them to feel like a crowd , &quot; Dewey @-@ Hagborg said of the portraits .
&quot; I wanted it to feel like a mass movement formed with Chelsea , like the movement that was also behind its liberation . &quot;
Professor of Northwestern University and an Associate of Oxford University for murder .
A nationwide human hunt is in progress for a Professor at Northwestern University and an Oxford University employee , who are considered suspicious after a man was assaulted in a luxury Chicago apartment .
On Monday Wyndham Lathem ( 42 ) and Andrew Warren ( 56 ) were issued arrest warrants for murder because of their alleged participation in the death of Trenton H. James Cornell @-@ Duranleau , as shown by the files of the Cook County Court .
The documents say that Cornell @-@ Duranleau , 26 , passed away after several stitches .
A joint warning system published by the Chicago Police Office states that the corpse was discovered on 27 July .
Officials received a call , arrived at the Grand Plaza Apartments and found the victim with several injuries to his body .
Cornell @-@ Duranleau was still declared dead in the place of events , and detectives investigate the bull as murder , while the police actively searches for the two suspects , said officials .
Lathem is an Associate Professor of Microbiology and Immunology at Northwestern University since 2007 .
Alan K. Cubbage , vice president of university relations , stated in an email statement that Lathem had been admitted to the University Campus and was not allowed to enter the University of Northwestern .
&quot; This is now a criminal matter , which is being investigated by the competent authorities , and Northwestern University cooperates with this investigation , &quot; Cubbage said .
Warren is Senior Treasury Assistant at Oxford University .
A speaker from the University and Somerville College said in an email statement that &quot; we are in contact with the UK police and are ready to assist the US investigating authorities in every way possible . &quot;
The statement added that Warren &apos;s colleagues were shocked and want him to stand up .
Chief Communications Officer of the Chicago Police Office , Anthony Guglielmi , said he urged the suspects to face the authorities .
&quot; The police have an idea of their place of residence , and our efforts to locate them are intensifying themselves , &quot; said Guglielmi .
Guglielmi said that local , regional and national authorities help to find the suspects .
Guglielmi said that the police received a call from the building manager of the Grand Plaza building who had just received an enigmatic tip saying that something had happened in apartment 1008 .
The police described the scene as very cruel .
Guglielmi said that it was unclear whether the incident had also taken place on July 27 .
It was confirmed by security cameras that Lathem and Warren were in the building .
&quot; We believe that Professor Latham and the victim had a relationship , &quot; Guglielmi said .
The management team at Grand Plaza published a statement to the residents : &quot; The police are currently working on the timeline and background of the victim and is exploring a variety of motives , including a possible domestic incident . &quot;
&quot; We will complete the WADA timetable in the near future &quot; - Russian Vice Premier Mutko .
The Russian Vice Premier Vitaly Mutko said that it won &apos;t be long before the remaining criteria of the World Anti @-@ Doping Agency ( WADA ) for the restoration of the Russian Anti @-@ Doping Agency ( RUSADA ) are implemented .
&quot; At a certain stage of meeting the criteria of the timetable RUSADA has been granted the right to plan and test in cooperation with UKAD ( UK Anti @-@ Doping ) .
The WADA timetable has been updated in this respect , &quot; Mutko said on Thursday .
The PM commented on the second part of the WADA Road Map for Compliance that describes the criteria for the reactivation of RUSADA and was recently published on the website of the organisation .
According to Mutko , there is nothing that could give Russia cause for concern .
&quot; Everything was announced , everything will be implemented .
And the results will be presented to the International Olympic Committee ( IOC ) and WADA in the near future , &quot; he added .
However , one of the criteria mentioned in the list states that the Russian anti @-@ doping authorities must publicly accept the reported results of the investigation approved by WADA into alleged state @-@ sponsored doping in Russian sport by Canadian Attorney Richard McLaren .
Regarding the matter , Mutko said : &quot; We are conducting the investigation because our anti @-@ doping system has admitted a mistake .
All measures have been implemented .
But there were no state programs , and we will not admit anything that does not exist . &quot;
Mutko &apos;s words were in agreement with those of Vitaly Smirnov , head of the independent Russian Anti @-@ Doping Commission .
In a conversation with the Russian RSport sales office at the beginning of the day , Smirnov admitted problems of the past in Russian anti @-@ doping organizations , but then added : &quot; We have repeatedly said that the report contains controversial positions and regulations .
Nobody intends to accept this report unconditionally , &quot; Smirnov added .
RUSADA was excluded from the practice of doping tests in Russia in November 2015 in the wake of the doping scandal .
However , it was allowed to plan and coordinate tests under the supervision of international experts and the UK Anti @-@ Doping ( UKAD ) .
After a visit of the Moscow headquarters of the organisation in July , WADA Director General Olivier Niggli declared that RUSADA was &quot; moving in the right direction &quot; in order to be reestablished .
