The rise of sex robots is real , and we should be worried .
Just when you thought it would not be possible to get crazy in 2017 , a new report will be published on the technological developments in the field of sex robots .
Yes , indeed .
Sex robots are currently a big thing .
Recently , the Foundation for Responsible Robotics ( FRR ) published a report on the development of sex robots over the next five to ten years .
According to Noel Sharkey , professor of robotics and artificial intelligence at the University of Sheffield and co @-@ founder of FRR , we must start to take their rise seriously .
Customers can choose the robot &apos;s eye color , shape of the breasted product and type of fingernail .
&quot; People are making fun of them , but companies are delivering a lot of it and we will see it much more often , &quot; said Mr. Sharkey when he published his new report .
Modern sex dolls have evolved from their inflatable partners into robots with a silicone skin that feels warm - with conscious human reactions , achieved by artificial intelligence .
The user can also &quot; customize &quot; his robot according to his / her convictions , choosing everything from the robot &apos;s eye color , the shape of the breastplate , to the type or color of his / her fingernails .
But it is even more worrying , as many robots own the &quot; personalities &quot; that would make a Stepford woman look progressive .
Modern sex dolls have developed into robots with a silicone skin .
RealBotix Robot allows users to adapt their robots to the properties they find appealing , such as timidity .
And then there are the True Companion Roxxxy Gold Sex Robots with pre @-@ programmed personalities like &quot; Frigid Farrah , &quot; which give the impression of shyness and &quot; Wild Wendy &quot; with an &quot; adventurous &quot; personality .
&quot; Roxxxy Gold has a personality that is as well adapted to your personality as possible , &quot; glows down the site of True Companion .
So she likes what you like , and she does not like what you do not like , etc .
She has her moods throughout the day - just like real people !
She can be tired , fixed to conversation or she can be &quot; in mood &quot; !
There are many worrying aspects to this rise of sex robots - not least because they replace real human relationships - but the submissive female properties , the references to rape , when one takes a step towards Frigid ( in this case : rebellious ) Farrah , are most troubling .
On his site compared True Companion Roxxxy with a vibrator , but for men .
&quot; If women ( sic ) can have a vibrator , why can &apos;t men have a roxxxy ? &quot; says the website .
However , these sex robots are not just fetishes or just another sexual toy .
Their origin and their growing refinement point to something darker and deeper in our culture , a withdrawal from the ideal of gender equality to a desire for sex with subjugation as an optional accessory .
Most men will not have sex robots , of course , and while FRR notes their growing popularity , they are still on the edge of consumer culture for the time being .
But what is leaking out of the peripheral areas can be very instructive in relation to the spirit of the time in which we live .
And many people are not strange or insulting until the free market gives them permission to do so .
There is a certain overlap that these highly developed sex robots are emerging at a time when women &apos;s rights are threatened worldwide , when there is a president in the White House who has boasted that he has sexually attacked women .
The most dissuasive aspect of The Handmaid &apos;s Tale ( The Report of the Magd ) is not the graphic images , the worn @-@ out body and the eyes , but how realistic this vision is .
The republic of Gilead is a jump , but for the moment this does not feel like a big jump .
The goal behind these sex robots is to create a physical resemblance to real women as realistically as possible ( though with pornostar proportions ) .
Their creators want them to feel human , to imitate the movement of a real body .
But , to put it in a nutshell , robots do not represent real women when it comes to their &quot; personalities . &quot;
You cannot detach yourself from your companion or simply leave .
They have no mediation or background story , nothing that indicates independence or anything that could disturb the imagination of total subjugation .
In other words , they are happy slaves .
Or , to put it in the language of 2017 , &quot; service maids . &quot;
Trumps great achievement ?
It makes Mitt Romney the embodiment of common sense .
It has become a truism of the Trump era that the political divisions that have polarized the US electorate have divided small @-@ sized families .
Around Christmas and Harvest Festival , the USA has had newspapers offering advice on how to deal with the horror of a colleague elected by the president .
We are all allegedly making efforts to have our filter bubbles burst .
Less has been noticed is the power of Trumps to bring families together .
I mention this because my cousin , a leftist poet who lives in Chicago and has been working with the Republicans in our family for a long time , visited me in New York this week .
She reminded me that unity against a common enemy can have a powerful effect .
With a whale @-@ house @-@ based of a political @-@ political kind , everyone who knows it , including the Republican family , is suddenly and uniquely on the same side , with a story about the politics of the country .
This is certainly a good thing about the dining table , but I notice in a broader context that this also involves considerable risks .
The left was strengthened by a strong and disfiguring impact of his presidency , but the power is to push us all to the right .
When we speak of normalization and of a tale of a man , we are referring to the scary possibility that one day his kittens will not repel us .
But there is an even more shocking long @-@ term scenario in which he &quot; normalizes &quot; right @-@ wing Republicans who suddenly appear to be the embodiment of rationality in comparison with his standards .
Today I find myself attacked by an active nostalgia for Mitt Romney &apos;s bizarre version of the crazy - the dog on the car roof , the 14 % income tax ( but at least we knew how his tax return looked ) - both of which are indeed very mild crimes compared to the one of Trumpf .
When he leaves , the next Republican candidate must be only mentally healthy to qualify as an immense improvement .
When my cousin was in the city , we brought our children to the Carousel in Central Park , the largest carousel in the New York Park Department , and the best three dollars to spend in the city if you don &apos;t need caffeine .
