Fund for Local Hearts III
If you want to restore your house , which has been restored over the years , you can get support from the country soon .
Mayor Albert Schindler and three representatives STEG Municipal Development informed about this on Wednesday in Empfingen .
At the beginning of the information event Schindler gave a second review of what had happened so far .
Since 1991 there have been areas of redevelopment in Empfingen .
At that time , in the redevelopment area I from 1991 to 2004 , the state of Baden @-@ Württemberg had taken over another two @-@ thirds of the funding .
In the recovery area II from 2005 to 2016 , the grant amounted to 60 % .
Schindler sees the previous redevelopment as a &quot; success project &quot; - after all , it is important to promote internal development as well , and not only to open up new construction areas .
On April 4 , the Karlsruhe Regional Council informed the reorganisation area III that there would be a redevelopment area .
The total amount of the project is 833 333 euros , of which 500 000 euros would be from the country , the rest from the municipality of Empfingen .
How does a remediation area now emerge ?
Schindler continued to investigate where the &quot; really old &quot; houses are .
But it also plays a role whether there is any interest in the planned area to restore .
If necessary , the area borders could be moved even further .
The STEG represented Martin Keller , Gaby Pietzschmann and Sarah Gotzel on Wednesday evening .
Keller presented the contents of the Federal @-@ Länder @-@ Programme &quot; Social City , &quot; in which the remediations would then be carried out .
The main focus of the programme is the revitalisation of inner cities , the improvement of living and working conditions and the maintenance and development of the infrastructure .
The measures would be carried out on an object @-@ based basis , i.e. per plot .
The area of redevelopment would then be defined as a statute .
The grant period for the funds will run from January 1 , 2017 to April 30 , 2026 .
By September of this year , however , the inventory would be drawn up , in which the participants in the redevelopment area would receive a questionnaire to fill out .
In November or December the decree of the Statutes should be made , if possible , so that the remediations can begin next year .
Pietzschmann then explained that each municipality must conduct the aforementioned preliminary investigations .
The aim is to assess the urban planning problems and to decide when and to what extent .
A reclamation note will then be entered in the land register for the respective property .
Pietzschmann promised that he would come to the &quot; Empfingen &quot; again and that he would get an idea of the situation .
Gotzel stressed that one of the key success factors for the project was the participation of the participants .
Therefore , there will be questionnaires that will be sent to citizens in the coming weeks and can be filled in by the end of the summer holidays .
The yellow questionnaire is the &quot; Building and Land Arch , &quot; which deals , among other things , with the construction condition and the plans for redevelopment .
The grey questionnaire , the &quot; Household and Household Arches , &quot; provides information on the size , the division and the inhabitants of a living room .
The blue &quot; operating arc &quot; can only be filled if the building has business premises .
However , Gotzel pointed out that a completed questionnaire is not a funding application at the same time .
In addition , new building measures are not eligible for funding .
Schindler also stressed that the distribution of funds works according to the &quot; greyhound principle &quot; - first come first , first serve .
You cannot &quot; reserve &quot; any funds for later .
Finally , photos of the project &quot; Village II &quot; were shown to make a &quot; tasty &quot; redevelopment for those present .
