The Advertising Costs of the White House Cost the Taxpayer Thousands
The decision of the White House to fly a naval helicopter to the South Lawn for an event that highlighted American production last month costs the tax @-@ payer up to $ 24,000 , according to the military data provided to TIME magazine .
The green @-@ white Sikorsky VH @-@ 3D , known as Marine One , when the president is on board , was the heart of the event on July 17 at the White House with American construction programs .
President Donald Trump , Vice @-@ President Mike Pence and senior White House officials made a tour of products from all 50 countries .
The helicopter , manufactured in Connecticut , was exhibited alongside a Maine yacht , a Wisconsin fire @-@ fighter car and a Mississippi forklift truck .
The Military Office of the White House requested the helicopter &apos;s presence in a fragmentary order or FRAGO , barely 36 hours before the helicopter landed on the South Lawn , according to the records of the Marine Helicopter Squadron One ( HMX @-@ 1 ) , the unit responsible for the helicopter &apos;s operation .
&quot; I just wanted you to be aware of this , because it is such an unusual event with high visibility , &quot; the commander of HMX @-@ 1 wrote on the eve of the event to his superior , the naval deputy for aviation .
The message was that the helicopter arrived at 7 a.m. on the South Lawn on July 17th for the event at 3 p.m. and stayed until the lawn was cleared between 6 p.m. and 9 p.m. that evening .
The note adds that if the departure from the White House should be delayed , a second crew for the return flight would be required because of the limitations of the working hours .
The original aircrew was on the helicopter during the event , while the unit &apos;s security staff was on the ground during the time .
The record provided by TIME did not make it clear whether a second flight crew was ultimately required .
The Hatch Act prohibits federal employees from using state property for political purposes .
Data records indicate that HMX @-@ 1 asked whether the event could violate the provision .
&quot; One question we asked was whether it was a violation of the Hatch Act and we were informed that this was not the case , &quot; the commander wrote .
&quot; Sounds as if you are locked , &quot; the Deputy Commander said .
The event &quot; Made in America &quot; was described by the White House as an official event and would not have been covered by the Hatch Act .
But official events also have political overtones .
At the event , the president gave a boost to the reform of health care in progress in the Senate and propagated efforts to reduce the government &apos;s rules .
The use of the aircraft known as Marine One or Air Force One for political benefits is hardly a new phenomenon .
Presidents are obliged to use it for the trip .
But to request their use only for a photo @-@ OP is unusual .
In February , he did an investigation when the presidential plane provided taxi services against the background of his first campaign rally in Melbourne , Florida , and his Twitter account is full of messages that were complaining about the use of the presidential plane by his predecessor .
&quot; The White House is enthusiastic about the show &quot; Made In America &quot; - which shows products from all 50 countries manufactured by American workers using American materials , &quot; said Lindsay Walters , Deputy Secretary of the White House .
HMX @-@ 1 crews frequently perform training flights in the area around Washington and the South Lawn to remove the US President from the White House with precise centimeters .
When he was at the German G20 summit in early July , HMX @-@ 1 performed 58 practice landings in the White House .
The flight for the &quot; Made in America &quot; event counted among the training needs of the flight crew for the month , said an official .
Helicopter units also flew 11 hours that day for &quot; non @-@ presidential support missions . &quot;
The White House said that the tax payers didn &apos;t take over the burden of any of the other props presented at the event .
A Sikorsky spokesman said that the company had not been involved in exposing the helicopter on the South Lawn .
HMX @-@ 1 does not keep budget records for the presidential flights , and it is difficult to determine the exact cost of the event .
According to hourly tariffs of the US Department of Defense for the financial year 2017 , the DoD refund rate for VH @-@ 3D is , however , 24.380 USD per flight hour .
The unit records the flight time of the aircraft as 30 minutes from the home base of the Marine Corps Air Facility in Quantico in Virginia .
The White House argues that the actual costs of helicopter operation are far below this rate .
&quot; Setting the costs for the tax payer on the basis of the estimations for the rates of reimbursement is highly misleading , &quot; said Walters .
&quot; These estimates include personnel , maintenance and many other hidden costs included in the annual funds . &quot;
According to a 2015 RAND study , DoD &apos;s refund rates do not include personnel costs , but take into account fuel , maintenance and contract costs .
At that time , Sean Spicer , former White House Press Secretary , defended the helicopter &apos;s use for the event .
&quot; The idea this week is to present things that are produced in America , &quot; Spicer said .
&quot; And I know that Sikorsky and the state of Connecticut are very proud that they contribute to our national security , and I assume that hundreds , if not thousands , of people depend on it .
And I think , like most Americans , we are all proud of the helicopter and other military equipment for which so many Americans have worked tirelessly .
It is of course appropriate to highlight this . &quot;
It was not clear whether he interacted with the helicopter when he entered his South Lawn tour for the event , but he sat in the driver &apos;s seat of a fire fighter car .
In the White House , he spoke to Sikorsky representatives and joked with the media about his own fleet of company products .
&quot; I know Sikorsky very well , &quot; the president said , &quot; I have three of them . &quot;
