The Afghan democracy depends on the political role of women , says the UN .
Elections can only be representative if all members of society , including women , play a role , said the head of the UN mission in Afghanistan on Wednesday .
Nicholas Haysom , the acting director of the United Nations Mission , said that hundreds of women will be standing in the provincial council elections , three women are candidates for the role of Vice President and more than 30 % of newly registered voters are women .
&quot; The role of women cannot be overestimated , &quot; he said in a statement on Wednesday .
